### Define Custom Console Styles

Source: https://symfony.com/doc/5.x/console/coloring.html

Create custom formatting styles using the OutputFormatterStyle class and register them with the output formatter.

```php
use Symfony\Component\Console\Formatter\OutputFormatterStyle;

// ...
$outputStyle = new OutputFormatterStyle('red', '#ff0', ['bold', 'blink']);
$output->getFormatter()->setStyle('fire', $outputStyle);

$output->writeln('<fire>foo</>');
```

--------------------------------

### Apply Built-in Console Styles

Source: https://symfony.com/doc/5.x/console/coloring.html

Use predefined tags to apply standard colors and background styles to console output.

```php
// green text
$output->writeln('<info>foo</info>');

// yellow text
$output->writeln('<comment>foo</comment>');

// black text on a cyan background
$output->writeln('<question>foo</question>');

// white text on a red background
$output->writeln('<error>foo</error>');
```

--------------------------------

### Apply ANSI colors to progress bar format

Source: https://symfony.com/doc/5.x/components/console/helpers/progressbar.html

Include ANSI codes or Symfony color tags within a format definition to style the output.

```php
ProgressBar::setFormatDefinition(
    'minimal',
    '<info>%percent%</info>\033[32m%\033[0m <fg=white;bg=blue>%remaining%</>'
);
```

### How to Color and Style the Console Output > Using Color Styles

Source: https://symfony.com/doc/5.x/console/coloring.html

If you need to display a tag literally in the output, you can escape it with a backslash or use the escape method to handle all tags within a string.

--------------------------------

### How to Color and Style the Console Output > Using Color Styles

Source: https://symfony.com/doc/5.x/console/coloring.html

You can apply styles to text by surrounding it with tags. The closing tag can be replaced by the generic </> tag to revoke all formatting. Custom styles can be defined using the OutputFormatterStyle class, which supports both named colors and hexadecimal color codes.

